# Post-quantum TLS (commercialization roadmap Phase 2 / Pillar 3.1): Caddy's
# own Go TLS stack doesn't yet negotiate a hybrid X25519+ML-KEM-768 key
# exchange for TLS 1.3 as of the version pinned in docker-compose.yml --
# there's no Caddyfile directive to opt into it because the underlying
# support isn't there yet. Track https://github.com/golang/go (the `crypto/tls`
# X25519MLKEM768 curve ID landed in Go 1.24; confirm Caddy's own Go
# toolchain/build has picked it up) and bump the pinned Caddy image once it
# has -- this then applies for free, no config change beyond the version bump.
#
# Until then, the effort-to-value winner (see docs/COMMERCIALIZATION_ROADMAP.md's
# Pillar 3.1) is putting a modern CDN/WAF in front of this reverse proxy
# instead: Cloudflare and comparable providers already offer hybrid
# X25519+ML-KEM-768 for TLS 1.3 today, no code or infra change here at all
# -- see docs/DEPLOYMENT_PQC.md.
{$DOMAIN:localhost} {
	reverse_proxy api:8000

	header {
		Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains"
	}
}
